CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--no-malloc-may-fail --dfcc main --apply-loop-contracts _ --unwindset callee.0:4 --unwinding-assertions
^\[callee.assigns.\d+\] line \d+ Check that h is assignable: FAILURE$
^\[callee.assigns.\d+\] line \d+ Check that g\[.*0\] is assignable: SUCCESS$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
Check that a is assignable
Check that k is assignable
--
Checks that the fix for callee-local variables in uncontracted loops does not
hide genuine frame violations: a write to a global that the caller's loop
assigns clause omits must still fail.
